# ============================================================================
# Orchestrator — what NEVER goes remote.
#
# The tree is ~88% local state by size (code+docs 4.6 MB, state 29.8 MB), so
# this file is the boundary that makes a repo viable at all. Owner's hard rules:
# no evaluation databases stored remotely, no reliance on remote access to work.
#
# Runtime state proper lives OUTSIDE this tree at $ORCH_STATE_DIR (default
# ~/.codex/orchestrator, ~20 GB: the Brain, cadence stamps, worktrees, venvs,
# the capability ledger). That separation is why a second instance needs only a
# different ORCH_STATE_DIR, not a code change.
#
# NOTE ON FORMAT: git does NOT support trailing comments on pattern lines. The
# first version of this file put explanatory comments after each pattern, which
# silently made every pattern inert — 795 files staged instead of 141, including
# the Brain export. Keep comments on their own lines, and verify with
# `git check-ignore -v` or `git status`, never with a hand-rolled parser.
# ============================================================================

# --- evaluation & experiment output: machine-local by the owner's explicit rule ---
# experiments/ is 17 MB / 390 files of per-arm logs, diffs and ship gates.
experiments/
# ux_reviews/ is 2.6 MB / 262 files of UX panel transcripts and scores.
ux_reviews/
# data/ holds feedback-snapshot.json (1.9 MB) — a Brain export, not source.
data/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
# GitHub rate-limit accounting for THIS machine only.
gh-rate-ledger.ndjson

# --- durable audit history belongs to the workspace, not the tool ---
# Code/Audits/Orchestrator/ is the system-of-record for dated decision records;
# capability_admission.commitments() reads it from there. A second copy here
# would be a parallel inventory — the failure mode this project is named for.
Audits/

# --- python / tooling noise ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- lock and backup artifacts ---
*.lock
*.bak
*.pre-ingest-fix-*

# --- editor / OS ---
.DS_Store
*.swp

# --- machine-local policy and evidence (the tool is public; the evidence is not) ---
# The split is tool-vs-evidence: generic capabilities and gates ship, while this
# instance's failure history, spend calibration and availability stay local.
# Sanitized public twins of the load-bearing docs are committed under their
# canonical names; these are the full versions.
LOCAL_POLICY.md
IMPROVEMENT_BACKLOG.md
CAPABILITY_USEFULNESS.md
*.local.md
